;*********************************************************************************************
; ByzBot v1.0 - Byzantine policy layer for AiBuilder
;*********************************************************************************************
;
; PURPOSE
;   Apply Byzantine counter-unit policy through AiBuilder's existing
;   desired-number-* goals. AiBuilder remains responsible for training.
;
; v1.0 SCOPE
;   - Enemy Archery Range -> increase skirmisher quota.
;   - Enemy Stable -> increase spearman quota.
;   - No direct train rules.
;   - No new goals.
;   - No scratch goals / temporary registers.
;   - No attack commands.
;   - No economic overrides.
;   - No unqualified enemy unit-count rule.
;
; IMPORTANT
;   The enemy-building predicate below is intentionally a runtime
;   qualification target. Its presence in this file is not evidence that
;   any-enemy semantics have already been proven in the AiByz runtime.
;
;   The phase system owns the baseline desired-number-* values. ByzBot
;   writes an override only when the observed condition is true.
;*********************************************************************************************

; Enemy ranged-production capability -> Byzantine skirmisher response.
(defrule
    (players-building-type-count any-enemy archery-range > 0)
=>
    (set-goal desired-number-skirmishers 12))

; Enemy cavalry-production capability -> Byzantine spearman response.
(defrule
    (players-building-type-count any-enemy stable > 0)
=>
    (set-goal desired-number-spearmen 10))

;*********************************************************************************************
; END ByzBot v1.0
;*********************************************************************************************
